<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-takahashii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila takahashii Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.362 µm (Pass 2 specimen composite) — MorphoEval overall 88.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Same Schnakenberg chart as Pass 1 (analytic λ = 2.3615 µm, measured 2.314 µm, Pearson r = 0.9905, KS = 0.0909, RMSE = 0.0568). The body mask is now the largest smoothed dark component (area 0.053, circularity 0.307, aspect 0.220) instead of the fragmented Otsu contour (circularity 0.0018). The GIF crossfades the lattice onto the gallery plate: 640×480, 12 frames, mean frame motion 0.068, CV similarity 93.5. Simulation coherency 0.269 versus specimen coherency 0.160. Equal-diffusion ablation still collapses. Age 0 Ma. Scale 2.362e-06 m. Overall 88.5/100 (faithfulness 88.7, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 12c1685418b29b353dac76e72a07fc55dd94800c; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_takahashii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-takahashii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 12c1685418b29b353dac76e72a07fc55dd94800c, image/png, 473535 B, 1512×912 px, artifact_sha256 9d1909ffe0bdfb85e18017066d942c34c767a7595c3ab007acf20b9f4670b5c6 (sha256 9d1909ffe0bdfb85e18017066d942c34c767a7595c3ab007acf20b9f4670b5c6), spec_fingerprint 55cc231a3a77c642a29cd527c03b6d6546b3cf3ea80c82a6ec4a040de441d66a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 55cc231a3a77c642a29cd527c03b6d6546b3cf3ea80c82a6ec4a040de441d66a; artifact_sha256: 9d1909ffe0bdfb85e18017066d942c34c767a7595c3ab007acf20b9f4670b5c6; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_takahashii_turing_wavelength_s0/Drosophila_takahashii_specimen.jpg=be067c44d300a455..., datasets/drosophila_takahashii_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_takahashii_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=c96d7a5d72c78239..., datasets/drosophila_takahashii_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=101832d102fd3942..., datasets/drosophila_takahashii_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=9b6681d3a2e6cbf4...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-takahashii-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 diffusion-driven instability and a finite critical wavelength | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics with a cubic autocatalytic term | Murray 1981 wavelength set by the diffusion scale | Tanaka, Barmina and Kopp 2009 and Kopp 2011 on sex-comb diversification | Atallah et al. 2014 on Drosophila suzukii and its close relatives; reconstructed_in_script: Parameters a=0.162, b=1.247, Du=0.042744, Dv=0.971570 placing λ_c at 2.362 µm | Smoothed 22nd-percentile body mask and the lattice-to-plate crossfade | Dispersion Pearson/KS, Dv sweep, and equal-diffusion ablation; transfer_boundary: 2.362e-06 m is the campaign detail-scale assignment (log10=-5.627), not a quoted takahashii ocellus measurement | The suzukii → takahashii → teissieri order is chronoseries index 37/41 at 0 Ma, not an anagenetic fossil series; does_not_claim: That a wet-lab paper reports 2.362 µm for a D. takahashii ocellus | That D. takahashii carries the D. suzukii apical wing spot | That the narrow dark core (area 0.053) is the entire fly silhouette." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=1.3]: Only one gallery plate is pinned. A second CC photograph of Drosophila takahashii was not found.",
        "remediation needed: R3. Still one gallery plate and one assessor. A second specimen and an independent scorer are not available in this run.",
        "remediation needed: R4. The 2.362 µm length remains the campaign scale assignment, not a wet-lab ocellus measurement. Do not replace it with an invented empirical table." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.85e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

